WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.100
Who's involved?

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.274
The vulnerability manager
owns the exposure gate:

3
00:00:04.274 --> 00:00:07.675
an owner for every exposed
device, and the weekly queue.

4
00:00:07.675 --> 00:00:10.998
The security operations lead
owns the incident gate:

5
00:00:10.998 --> 00:00:14.775
a daily queue review, and every
overdue incident owned today.

6
00:00:14.775 --> 00:00:17.928
The security officer files
the Exposure Management

7
00:00:17.928 --> 00:00:21.512
disposition in the closure
register, and the inventory gaps.

8
00:00:21.512 --> 00:00:24.525
One caution: the incident
check only reads.

9
00:00:24.525 --> 00:00:28.313
It never assigns, comments
on or closes an incident.

10
00:00:28.313 --> 00:00:31.783
And the severity strings the
exposure query filters on are

11
00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:34.970
as the portal shows them;
check them in the test tenant.
